<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Required because we sign with the hardened runtime.

         Under hardened runtime macOS does not merely refuse a privacy protected
         resource without these keys. It refuses SILENTLY: no prompt is drawn,
         no error is returned, and the authorization status simply stays
         `notDetermined` forever. That failure looks identical to a missing
         usage string or a broken TCC row, which is what made it slow to find.
         The usage strings in Info.plist are necessary but not sufficient; both
         halves have to be present.

         An existing grant can mask a missing entitlement, because the request
         short circuits instead of asking. Verify each capability on a clean
         grant, not one inherited from an earlier build.

         Note for future edits: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen.
         AMFI rejects the whole file with "syntax error" if one appears. -->

    <!-- EventKit. Calendar and Reminders both sit behind this one key. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- CNContactStore. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- NSAppleScript driving Notes.app, and later Messages.app. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
